common/ is FreeBSD's sys/compat/linuxkpi/common, unmodified:

	https://github.com/freebsd/freebsd-src
	commit c30a321a61ce7e1c03d4c314b2127b37f75564c6 (2026-10-14)

dummy/ is sys/compat/linuxkpi/dummy from the same commit, unmodified: stub
headers searched after common/include, as in FreeBSD's kmod.mk.

Only the sources needed for PCIe wifi drivers (rtw88) were imported; the
remaining common/src files (USB, I2C, HDMI, ACPI, DMI, shmemfs, ...) were left
out on purpose. All of common/include was imported, as headers pull in each
other freely.

haiku/fbsd_subr_pctrie.c and haiku/compat/sys/{pctrie,_pctrie}.h are FreeBSD's
sys/kern/subr_pctrie.c and sys/sys/{pctrie,_pctrie}.h from the same commit,
unmodified. So are haiku/compat/sys/tree.h (FreeBSD's sys/sys/tree.h), which
LinuxKPI's <linux/rbtree.h> builds the Linux rb-tree API on, and
haiku/compat/sys/{_bitset,bitset,_cpuset,cpuset}.h (cpuset_t, whose layout
linux_compat.c's cpumask code relies on).

To update, copy the same file set from a newer commit and rebuild.
